WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.738
One point two billion dollars in political money.

00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:05.340
Six point two million donation records.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.113
Three hundred and fifty thousand lobbying contacts.

00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:11.829
Three thousand, one hundred and thirty-three government contracts.

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:13.727
Six datasets, cross-linked.

00:00:13.727 --> 00:00:15.206
This is the machine.

00:00:15.206 --> 00:00:17.988
The cross-reference engine matches timelines.

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:19.068
Who met whom.

00:00:19.068 --> 00:00:20.102
When they met.

00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:21.284
How they voted.

00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:22.261
Who donated.

00:00:22.261 --> 00:00:23.556
Who got the contract.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:29.272
The revolving door — corporate board to Parliament to lobbying firm and back to the board — is not a metaphor.

00:00:29.272 --> 00:00:32.159
It is a documented pattern with names and dates.

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:40.068
MP spotlight cards show individual members with their party affiliation, voting history, lobbying contacts received, and donations accepted.

00:00:40.068 --> 00:00:46.579
The methodology is simple: take the government's own data from six different databases and put it on the same page.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.420
The pattern reveals itself.
